    "status": "submitted",
    "answer": "To receive an SBIR award, the company must qualify as a small business concern at the time of award: it must be for-profit; have a U.S. place of business; operate primarily in the U.S. or significantly contribute to the U.S. economy; meet U.S. ownership and control rules (normally, over 50% directly owned and controlled by eligible U.S. citizens/permanent residents and/or qualifying small businesses); and have no more than 500 employees including affiliates. Certain agencies may apply an SBIR-specific exception for firms majority-owned by multiple venture-capital, hedge-fund, or private-equity companies.",
